WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.960
Marsha Holland and her husband… this guy... gave&nbsp;
birth to their daughter Barbara on September 13th,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:09.520
1967. They appear to be loving and doting&nbsp;
parents, treasuring all of their photos of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:12.400
her after her after her disappearance... even in the bathroom. In&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:16.160
an interview with W, actress Shannon Purser&nbsp;
revealed that these are actual photos from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:19.760
her youth, which were also part of a shrine&nbsp;
dedicated to her character at Comic-Con.

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:23.600
But despite the love Barb gets in our world,&nbsp;
she’s more of an afterthought in the world of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:27.520
Stranger Things in Hawkins, Indiana where she&nbsp;
grew up. To see what caused her to become a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:31.200
bit of an outcast in their community,&nbsp;
stick around the end of this video.

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:36.320
(mysterious music)

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:39.520
In her youth, Barb’s best friend was&nbsp;
Nancy Wheeler. While it’s never stated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:42.640
when Barb met Nancy, it’s assumed&nbsp;
to be a long lasting friendship. 
 &nbsp;

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:46.880
Since Barb has her own car in high school, she&nbsp;
oftentimes ends up as the designated driver for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:51.120
Nancy, like when the pair went shopping&nbsp;
for clothes in November 1983. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:54.560
despite the fact the fact that they still consider&nbsp;
each other as best friends, it’s clear that they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.560 --> 00:00:59.360
are beginning to drift apart before the events&nbsp;
of the story begin. Stranger Things is, at its core,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:03.600
about growing up in the 80s, and growing up&nbsp;
means finding out who you are, and it seems that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:08.080
the two find out that Barb is a lot more based&nbsp;
than Nancy. She wears the clothes she wants to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:12.480
wear, and honors her own values, not letting peer&nbsp;
pressure influence her decisions or thinking.

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:15.680
Nancy, on the other hand, expands&nbsp;
her horizons in high school. She&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:18.560
starts hanging out with different&nbsp;
people and participates in riskier&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:21.440
activities in order to impress a&nbsp;
boy she likes, Steve Harrington.

00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:23.100
– It's faberge organics.

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:23.600
– [Zac] On the morning&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:27.760
of November 7th, Barb is trying to pry details&nbsp;
out of Nancy about how things are going with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.760 --> 00:01:31.600
Steve. While supporting Nancy’s&nbsp;
feelings, she simultaneously teases Nancy and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:35.200
jokingly requests that Nancy doesn’t forget&nbsp;
about her, which is perhaps a projection of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:39.600
her worries that Nancy will move on and she’ll&nbsp;
be left behind, alone. She’s realizing that she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:44.320
isn’t as much of a priority in her best friend’s&nbsp;
mind as she once was, and that idea scares her.

00:01:44.320 --> 00:01:47.920
Nancy discovers a note from Steve in her&nbsp;
locker. Despite the concern over Nancy’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:51.680
newly growing popularity, Barb plays it&nbsp;
cool, and seems to be excited for her.
 &nbsp;

00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:55.520
She respects Nancy’s decisions and trusts her&nbsp;
to be smart enough to make her own choices.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.520 --> 00:01:59.840
This dynamic changes on Tuesday evening when&nbsp;
Nancy decides to go to Steve’s house party. Barb&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:03.920
receives a call from her, pleading for a ride.&nbsp;
Barb’s response is firmly against sneaking out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:07.760
to the party and lying to her parents, but&nbsp;
Nancy is insistent on dragging her along.
 &nbsp;

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:11.600
In the car, Barb criticizes Nancy’s decisions&nbsp;
on going while insisting that Steve only cares&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:15.200
about getting in her pants and that Nancy’s&nbsp;
not this stupid. There may be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:19.280
some real concern that Steve could be using&nbsp;
her, but a lot of this argument seems to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:23.360
rooted in jealousy. Caught between wanting to be&nbsp;
a good friend and her disdain towards the party,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:26.240
she still attends, even if it’s&nbsp;
only to keep an eye on Nancy.
 &nbsp;

00:02:26.240 --> 00:02:29.120
The party once again shows how the&nbsp;
two friends are just going in opposite&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:32.320
directions in life while trying to hold&nbsp;
onto each other because of their past.

00:02:32.320 --> 00:02:35.280
Nancy’s pressures her to shotgun a&nbsp;
beer and Barb hesitantly takes the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:38.400
can and pocket knife to try and punch a&nbsp;
hole in the bottom of it. Unfortunately,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:42.560
the knife slips and slices into her thumb instead,&nbsp;
and she rushes to the bathroom to clean up.
 &nbsp;

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:47.280
She returns to discover Nancy, soaking wet,&nbsp;
wrapped in a towel, and going upstairs -- THE&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:50.594
SAME PLACE SHE TRIED TO WARN NANCY THAT&nbsp;
STEVE WOULD TAKE HER. 

00:02:52.160 --> 00:02:56.000
– Why don’t you go ahead and go home.&nbsp;
I’ll just… I’ll get a ride or something.

00:02:56.720 --> 00:02:57.520
– Nance.

00:02:57.520 --> 00:02:59.200
– Barb.
– Donkey!

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:03.120
– [Zac] Barb tries to say that Nancy’s new behaviour&nbsp;
isn’t really her, because she’s in denial of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:07.120
the fact that this IS the new Nancy; she’s not&nbsp;
going to stay as she was as a kid forever. 
 &nbsp;

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:10.720
Rather than leaving, Barb decides to go back&nbsp;
outside and sit on the diving board to dip her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.720 --> 00:03:14.800
feet in the pool and reflect. Get it? Reflect?&nbsp;
Cause the pool has a reflection-- She has no&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:18.800
reason to stay at Steve’s anymore, but maybe&nbsp;
her sense of loyalty to Nancy keeps her there,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:22.080
hoping to offer her a ride home later&nbsp;
so they can make up. Or maybe she’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:25.117
just trying to listen in on her friend&nbsp;
getting drilled in the upstairs bedroom.

00:03:25.117 --> 00:03:26.501
– You know, you're so cute when you lie.

00:03:26.501 --> 00:03:27.280
– [Zca] We may never&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.280 --> 00:03:31.600
find out what her true intentions are, because a&nbsp;
droplet of blood falls from Barb’s hand into the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:36.160
pool and attracts the Demogorgon, which attacks&nbsp;
her and drags her into the alternate realm known&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.160 --> 00:03:41.120
as the Upside Down just as Steve Harrington turns&nbsp;
Nancy’s virginity upside-down. When Barb wakes up,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:45.200
she finds herself in the bottom of the pool,&nbsp;
but it’s empty and covered in strange vines.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:49.440
She’s bleeding and trying to figure out where&nbsp;
she is, instinctively calling out for Nancy.

00:03:49.440 --> 00:03:53.760
The upside down is a cold, isolated realm&nbsp;
devoid of human life. One of the only sounds&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:57.840
you’re likely to hear there, is your own voice&nbsp;
echoing back at you. I find it interesting that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:02.160
the Demogorgon takes its victims there when they&nbsp;
are at lonely, vulnerable point. For Will Byers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:05.440
it’s after an argument breaks out among the&nbsp;
friends about the outcome of their game of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.440 --> 00:04:08.960
Dungeons and Dragons which ultimately breaks&nbsp;
up the game, and for Barb it comes for her at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.960 --> 00:04:13.920
her loneliest point. Maybe the upside down is&nbsp;
a representation of the feeling of being alone.

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:19.351
When Barb turns around, she finds herself&nbsp;
face to… flower thing… with the Demogorgon.

00:04:20.138 --> 00:04:21.138
(growl)

00:04:21.138 --> 00:04:22.222
(scream)

00:04:22.222 --> 00:04:24.222
(impact)

00:04:27.114 --> 00:04:30.862
(brooding music)

00:04:30.862 --> 00:04:34.800
After finding herself trapped with the&nbsp;
terrifying monster in the upside-down version&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:36.479
of the Harringtons’ pool, Brab f--

00:04:36.884 --> 00:04:37.384
Brab!

00:04:37.384 --> 00:04:38.234
(laughter)

00:04:38.234 --> 00:04:41.117
...Barb frantically starts&nbsp;
clamoring around to find a way out. Eventually,

00:04:41.117 --> 00:04:45.840
she finds the ladder and makes it up to the edge&nbsp;
as she screams for Nancy. The Demogorgon grabs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:49.920
and drags Barb back into the pool. She tries to&nbsp;
hold onto the top of the ladder but eventually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.920 --> 00:04:54.000
loses grip and is yanked towards the bottom.&nbsp;
With her final scream for her friend cut off,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:58.640
she becomes the next victim of the Demogorgon.
 
For Nancy and the citizens of Hawkins, Barb is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.640 --> 00:05:02.640
declared a runaway after Nancy steps forward&nbsp;
to talk with police. While Nancy is adamant&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.640 --> 00:05:06.720
that Barb is missing, the officers Callahan and&nbsp;
Powell inform her, as they’re getting her story,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.720 --> 00:05:11.040
that Barb’s car wasn’t where Nancy claimed it&nbsp;
was, leading them to believe she’d skipped town.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:14.160
Callahan later tells Chief Hopper that&nbsp;
some guys from the state found the car.

00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:19.280
– [Callahan] Oh hey, they found Barbara’s car.
– [Hopper] What?&nbsp;

00:05:19.280 --> 00:05:22.800
– [Powell] Barbara Holland’s car.&nbsp;
Seems she ran away after all.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:25.440
Staties found it late last night at&nbsp;
the bus station.

00:05:25.440 --> 00:05:29.440
– [Zac] He’s referring to the Indiana State Police, but&nbsp;
it was obviously not Barb who drove it there.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.440 --> 00:05:33.600
This is the work of the Hawkins Lab, who is trying&nbsp;
to cover up the two disappearances from the town,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.600 --> 00:05:36.960
as not to raise suspicion. It is their&nbsp;
efforts, in combination with the fact&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.960 --> 00:05:41.200
that Barb was never very popular to begin with,&nbsp;
that are the reason she’s forgotten so fast by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.200 --> 00:05:46.480
the public -- the reason fans in the real world&nbsp;
started the online movement: #justiceforbarb.

00:05:46.480 --> 00:05:49.600
The next people to see Barb are Will&nbsp;
and Eleven. When Will wakes up in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.600 --> 00:05:52.480
the Demogorgon’s nest, he sees&nbsp;
her body encased in the sticky,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.480 --> 00:05:56.240
web-like substance with a slug crawling&nbsp;
out of her mouth. Eleven eventually uses&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.240 --> 00:06:00.720
her astral projection power and finds her at&nbsp;
Nancy’s request, confirming that Barb is dead.

00:06:00.720 --> 00:06:04.400
With the real cause of Barb’s death&nbsp;
being related to supernatural phenomena,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.400 --> 00:06:07.840
Nancy and everyone who knows the truth&nbsp;
had to swear they wouldn’t tell anyone,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.840 --> 00:06:11.360
or the government would step in. This&nbsp;
adds tension between Nancy and Steve,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.360 --> 00:06:14.640
because she starts grappling with the&nbsp;
guilt of Barb’s death being her fault.
 &nbsp;

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:19.200
Unfortunately, the “official” story of Barb&nbsp;
being a runaway gives a false hope to Mr. and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.200 --> 00:06:23.200
Mrs. Holland that they’ll be able to see their&nbsp;
daughter again. However, this story is easier for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.200 --> 00:06:27.360
the town to accept and brush aside without much&nbsp;
thought. Since she’s only really seen hanging out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.360 --> 00:06:33.840
with Nancy and since she’s an only child, most of&nbsp;
the town doesn’t actually notice that she’s gone.

00:06:33.840 --> 00:06:40.720
– [Barb] You forget about something? You forget about Old&nbsp;
Barb? Nancy’s friend? … Trapped in the ****ing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.720 --> 00:06:43.407
Upside-Down for the past two months?
– [Jimmy Kimmel] Alright, Barb…

00:06:43.407 --> 00:06:48.480
– [Barb] NA-NA-NA-NA-NAH! … There were two people&nbsp;
down there. And you rescued one of them.

00:06:48.480 --> 00:06:52.000
– [Zac] The lack of attention to her is partially&nbsp;
because the news of Will Byers returning from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:56.560
the dead is a bigger headline, and partly from her&nbsp;
seeming to be a loner when she’s not with Nancy.

00:06:56.560 --> 00:07:00.800
I should note that many people in town were&nbsp;
probably willing to accept the “runaway” story&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.800 --> 00:07:05.280
so easily thanks to the 1974 Runaway Youth&nbsp;
Act, which assisted runaways and provided&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.280 --> 00:07:09.440
resources and information on community food&nbsp;
banks, shelters, and other services. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:09.440 --> 00:07:13.920
also kept her parents hopeful for as long as they&nbsp;
were, which takes a sad turn the following year.
 &nbsp;

00:07:13.920 --> 00:07:18.640
At a Kentucky Fried dinner with Barb’s parents&nbsp;
in 1984, Nancy discovers that the Hollands&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.640 --> 00:07:22.640
are selling their house to pay a private&nbsp;
detective named Murray Bauman to find Barb.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.640 --> 00:07:26.240
Discovering this makes Nancy feel guilt&nbsp;
about the lack of closure for the Hollands,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:26.240 --> 00:07:29.920
and she devises a plan with help from&nbsp;
Jonathan Byers and Detective Bauman.

00:07:29.920 --> 00:07:33.760
She creates a tape that captures Dr. Owens,&nbsp;
the director of operations at the lab,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:33.760 --> 00:07:36.320
admitting that Barb’s death was&nbsp;
linked to the lab. This way,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.320 --> 00:07:40.320
they can craft a believable story that won’t&nbsp;
likely get them on any government hit list.

00:07:40.320 --> 00:07:44.080
Rather than proposing that Barb died of&nbsp;
supernatural causes, they go with a storyline&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.080 --> 00:07:48.480
about her disappearance being part of a conspiracy&nbsp;
to hide an experimental chemical asphyxiant leak&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.480 --> 00:07:52.240
that was from the lab. By basing it on something&nbsp;
familiar and terrifying, they are able to get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.240 --> 00:07:56.480
the support of the media and the public, and&nbsp;
get Hawkins Laboratory shut down. In doing so,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:56.480 --> 00:08:00.560
the Hollands must accept that Barb is gone and&nbsp;
finally hold a funeral for her.

00:08:00.560 --> 00:08:04.080
Barb Holland was a good natured girl,&nbsp;
who simply wanted to protect her friend&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.080 --> 00:08:07.440
from the dangers of peer pressure, but&nbsp;
ended up becoming a victim of it herself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.440 --> 00:08:10.320
in doing so. But other than that&nbsp;
one night, she was pretty based,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.320 --> 00:08:14.240
and her story is a sad example of how a tragedy&nbsp;
can be spun to push some kind of narrative.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:14.240 --> 00:08:18.200
So I’m just gonna spill some out for&nbsp;
Barb. Justice for Barb. This is water.

00:08:18.200 --> 00:08:19.200
(weird noise)

00:08:19.200 --> 00:08:22.320
I’m gonna be covering more Stranger&nbsp;
Bois here on Horror History,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.320 --> 00:08:25.200
so if you have any self-respect&nbsp;
at all, check out that playlist&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:25.200 --> 00:08:28.880
on the left and remember to subscribe&nbsp;
to CZsWorld for new horrors every week,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.880 --> 00:08:35.567
RING that deathbell for notifications and I’ll&nbsp;
see you in the next one. Assuming we both survive.

00:08:35.567 --> 00:08:38.956
(synth music)

00:08:38.956 --> 00:08:40.319
– FOR BARB!

